affolds.</article-title><source>Nat Methods. In press.</source></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001211-Webb1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Webb</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hitchcock</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Smeal</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Cyclic strain increases fibroblast proliferation, matrix accumulation, and elastic modulus of fibroblast-seeded polyurethane constructs.</article-title><source>J Biomech</source><volume>39</volume><fpage>1136</fpage><lpage>1144</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16256125</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001211-Kim1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Nikolovski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonadio</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mooney</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Cyclic mechanical strain regulates the development of engineered smooth muscle tissue.</article-title><source>Nat Biotech</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>979</fpage><lpage>983</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>Grants-in-Aid 18680039 and 19659503 from JSPS and young investigator grant from COE program.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>